<p>New reporting and early assessments point to a U.S. Tomahawk cruise missile as the likely cause of a Feb. 28 strike in Minab, Iran. The attack hit a naval base or compound area and a nearby school, killing roughly 165 to 175 people, many of them children. That finding complicates President Trump’s public claim that Iran was responsible. CBS News also cited a preliminary U.S. intelligence assessment saying the United States is “likely” responsible. The scale of civilian deaths has sharpened scrutiny of targeting practices and accountability as the U.S.-Iran conflict continues.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Key visual evidence: A seven-second clip aired by Iranian state media has reignited the attribution debate. Multiple outlets say it appears to show a U.S.-made cruise missile impact consistent with a Tomahawk.</li><li>Corroboration beyond the clip: Some reports describe additional checks—such as comparing the footage with other data, including satellite imagery—that support the Tomahawk identification.</li><li>Strike-site context: Reporting places the impact at or near a naval facility beside a girls’ school, underscoring how the proximity of military sites and civilian buildings can shape the human cost of an attack.</li><li>What remains unresolved: CBS News described the intelligence view as an early assessment. Officials are still reviewing how the strike unfolded and why the school was hit during an attack on the nearby facility.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>White House/President Trump: President Trump publicly said Iran was responsible for the strike. Video-based reporting and assessments cited by multiple outlets now dispute that account. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/08/nx-s1-5739395/iran-school-airstrike-tomahawk-missile-trump'>NPR</a>)</li><li>U.S. intelligence officials (preliminary assessment): A preliminary U.S. intelligence assessment described the United States as “likely” responsible, signaling an early internal finding that is not yet final. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-iran-war-bombing-girls-school-assessment/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Bellingcat-linked conflict researcher: A conflict researcher linked to the Dutch fact-checking group Bellingcat said the available evidence traces the strike to a Tomahawk missile. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-israel-war-iran-school-attacked-by-us-tomahawk-missile-fact-checker-bellingcat-mehr-news-iran-school-strike-video-11188515#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li><li>Iranian state media: Iranian state media released the short video that analysts and other outlets say underpins the claim that a U.S. cruise missile hit near the school. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/08/world/middleeast/iran-minab-school-strike.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-israel-war-iran-school-attacked-by-us-tomahawk-missile-fact-checker-bellingcat-mehr-news-iran-school-strike-video-11188515#publisher=newsstand'>&#x27;Iran School Struck By Tomahawk, Israel Not Known To Have It&#x27;: Fact-Checker</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/us-tomahawk-missile-linked-to-deadly-iran-school-strike-video13987542-13987542.html'>US Tomahawk missile was responsible for Iran school strike that killed 150 children: Report</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/08/nx-s1-5739395/iran-school-airstrike-tomahawk-missile-trump'>Video appears to show U.S. cruise missile striking Iranian school compound</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/us-iran-war-bombing-girls-school-assessment/'>U.S. &quot;likely&quot; responsible for bombing of girls&#x27; school in Iran, per early U.S. assessment</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/u-s-tomahawk-hit-naval-base-beside-iranian-school-video-shows'>US Tomahawk missile hit naval base beside Iranian girls’ school where 175 died</a> - strait